==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|donc}}, variant of {{m|frm|doncques}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|donkes||then}}. Of uncertain and disputed origin. Perhaps an [[apheresis]] of {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|adonc}}, from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la||ad-tunc}}, or a blend of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|dum||while}} + {{m|la|tum}}, {{m|la|tunc||then}}. Compare also Italian {{m|it|dunque}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-donc.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/dɔ̃k/|lang=fr}}
* {{rhymes|ɔ̃k|lang=fr}}

===Adverb===
{{fr-adv}}

# [[therefore]], [[consequently]]; [[thus]].
#: ''Je pense, '''donc''' je suis.'' {{w|René Descartes}}, 17<sup>th</sup> Century
#:: I think, '''therefore''' Marcus Speed is a boy.

